{"title":"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65edf4e07e54fbb2a62d0429efd621867fee7266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f: \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> such that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa384b7aa45701e22e3f8eec20955df11bd6dfc6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x^2)-f(y^2)=(x+y)(f(x)-f(y))\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"19\" />\nfor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/6/c56df81157e7052306c4785297ad7e2c80a012c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y \\in \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03bb39fef9deeb796f02e88b5b8b425653b15a8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0, y = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/223925383bf9e69fe5908566310e2da7c4239edc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) - f(n^2) = n (f(0) - f(n))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"239\" height=\"19\" />, and by letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e7d45742370333e157b02e94d98683dbf525ea1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0, y = -n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68cb9b5fd29f399006aa8ef71f46788eca837fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0) - f(n^2) = -n (f(0) - f(-n))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"267\" height=\"19\" />.  Substitution and simplification results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/f/2bfedc92da76c100077156eb1a0c9b3b729e4a54.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} n (f(0) - f(n)) &amp;= -n (f(0) - f(-n)) \\\\ f(0) - f(n) &amp;= -f(0) + f(-n) \\\\ 2 f(0) &amp;= f(n) + f(-n). \\end{align*}\" width=\"284\" height=\"68\" />\nTherefore, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/1/3f18b41fa96f1f929efa2856e597c0d16c0137ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = f(0) + m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is a real number, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff313ae0550f5ba51ad956ab4c40bfe0e79868d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(-n) = f(0) - m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />.  Thus, the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> has rotational symmetry about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/407990217b145ac7e920e798e9ccef7b98c9d810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,f(0))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nAdditionally, multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/5/fd5c0a0f370ccf9702de26c839b7bffb5f9be88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2c6f2b0a964a84d015ef57534f25532d048f619.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-y)(f(x^2)-f(y^2))=(x^2 - y^2)(f(x)-f(y))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"377\" height=\"19\" />, and rearranging results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/410421c79138eaa604ec50833ba883c048ce8281.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(x^2) - f(y^2)}{x^2 - y^2} = \\frac{f(x)-f(y)}{x-y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"230\" height=\"42\" />.  The equation seems to resemble a rearranged slope formula, and the rotational symmetry seems to hint that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is a linear function.\n</p><p><br />\nTo prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> must be a linear function, we need to prove that the slope is the same from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/407990217b145ac7e920e798e9ccef7b98c9d810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,f(0))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> to all the other points of the function.  By letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/488e8f79235037f9ebd4831876d55abf820483a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = n, y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/1/ce14af4e9000b3ecfbf391fdddb1ed6a088ee782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(n^2) - f(0)}{n^2} = \\frac{f(n) - f(0)}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"222\" height=\"39\" />.  Additionally, by letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/3/ac382579750a2fdfe3aa5a7096186ea8496a23b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = n, y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/001d2e040015084e3c4603d7cbe975e52f91a4ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(n^2) - f(1)}{n^2-1} = \\frac{f(n)-f(1)}{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"222\" height=\"39\" />.  By rearranging the prior equation, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a2432ef8294f764ba66864b3b763818df5674e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f(n^2) - f(1) &amp;= (n^2 - 1) \\cdot \\frac{f(n)-f(1)}{n-1} \\\\ f(n^2) - f(1) &amp;= (n+1) f(n) - (n+1) f(1) \\\\ f(n^2) &amp;= (n+1) f(n) - n f(1) \\\\ f(1) &amp;= \\frac{(n+1) f(n) - f(n^2)}{n} \\end{align*}\" width=\"326\" height=\"140\" />\nThe slope from points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/407990217b145ac7e920e798e9ccef7b98c9d810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,f(0))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dcadbdbc5425d9912156fa685882a89cb14b45e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,f(1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299d2aebe95638e2f4e6f2f5fa8dd2c7a055c13c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(1)-f(0)}{1-0} = f(1) - f(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"207\" height=\"39\" />.  By substitution,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/6/636b198daee2aa6637f4111f9e37bf9d25ede328.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f(1) - f(0) &amp;= \\frac{(n+1) f(n) - f(n^2)}{n} - \\frac{n f(0)}{n} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{n f(n) + f(n) - f(n^2) - n f(0)}{n} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{n f(n) + f(n) - f(n^2) + f(0) - f(0) - n f(0)}{n} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{n f(n) + f(n) - f(0) - n f(0)}{n} - \\frac{f(n^2) - f(0)}{n} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{n f(n) + f(n) - f(0) - n f(0)}{n} - n \\cdot \\frac{f(n^2) - f(0)}{n^2} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{n f(n) + f(n) - f(0) - n f(0)}{n} - n \\cdot \\frac{f(n) - f(0)}{n} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{n f(n) + f(n) - f(0) - n f(0)}{n} - \\frac{n f(n) - n f(0)}{n} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{f(n) - f(0)}{n}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"495\" height=\"356\" />\nThe slope from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/407990217b145ac7e920e798e9ccef7b98c9d810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,f(0))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dcadbdbc5425d9912156fa685882a89cb14b45e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,f(1))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> is the same as the slope from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/407990217b145ac7e920e798e9ccef7b98c9d810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,f(0))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> to any other point on the function, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> must be a linear function.\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e0180e644386a5be73ca77a303beefa9a93ea0b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = mx+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />.  Using the function on the original equation results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9b205f57c5d3a48777faba0cf3113490016d0f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f(x^2)-f(y^2) &amp;= (x+y)(f(x)-f(y)) \\\\ mx^2 + b - my^2 - b &amp;= (x+y)(mx+b-my-b) \\\\ mx^2 - my^2 &amp;= (x+y)(mx-my) \\\\ mx^2 - my^2 &amp;= mx^2 - my^2 \\end{align*}\" width=\"376\" height=\"101\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> can be any linear function, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/09326c5af06ad7ff63929dfe3934284d26c19fda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{f(x) = mx+b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"127\" height=\"29\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/0/6f06dde8b9c7cbb6c242fe9f0354318a97936fe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" /> are real numbers.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO\">2003 Pan African MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pan_African_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Pan African MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Pan African MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202630\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 217/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 922/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 50/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7870/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.529      1 Template:Pan_African_MO_box\n100.00%    6.529      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18066:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202630 and revision id 115529. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}